            "review_title": "Review at Conservo - Japanese Breads & Cafe",
            "review_text": "Edmund K\nSingapore, Singapore2883 contributions\n0\nA decent Japanese-styled bakery in HCMC.\nJan 2025 • Solo\nThis \"Japanese\" bakery is situated next to my hotel. I had wanted to pickup some buns for the night.\n\nHaving stayed, lived, worked and studied in Japan, Japanese breads are known for freshness, taste, creativity and presentation. \n\nConservo is a good attempt at catering Japanese breads to HCMC. Vietnam, from its historical links with France, already had experience with bread-making. The freshness of Conservo has to come from the ingredients and skills, and leadership of the baker.\n\nI wouldn't say Conservo is exactly en par with those in Japan. But the quality is better than Vietnamese bakery.\n\nI bought a sweet raisin bread, almond croissant and a custard raspberry pie.\n\nThe bakery has a cafe as well, where you can enjoy a cup of coffee with their bread.\nRead more\nWritten February 2, 2025",
